> Sign changes and the endpoint policy

For ordinates0,1,−100 at x=0,1,2, the initial middle tangent is negative despite
the first interval's positive secant. The producer clamps it before computing
the radial norm. The legacy limiter computed ratios before clamping and could
restore a wrong-sign tangent during its subsequent scaling; this is corrected.
The final middle tangent is zero, so the local maximum is respected. A second
panel zooms around that maximum while the first retains the complete curve and
endpoint clamps.

Finite queries outside the node range now return the nearest endpoint ordinate,
matching the documented clamping contract. The legacy implementation only
clamped its interval index and then extrapolated the cubic. Nonfinite queries
throw. These endpoint and sign-change fixes are intentional behavior
corrections; they are not hidden by the original monotone example.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/monotone_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::algorithms::MonotoneCubic c({0, 1, 2}, {0, 1, -100});
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (int i = 0; i <= 160; ++i) {
        double q = -1 + i / 40.0;
        x.push_back(q);
        y.push_back(c.evaluate(q));
    }
    std::print("Actual middle tangent: {}. First interval right-clamped: {}.\n\n| finite query | native " "value |\n| ---: | ---: |\n",
               c.tangents()[1], c.decisions()[0].right_clamped);
    for (double q : {-1., 0., .5, 1., 1.5, 2., 3.})
        std::print("| {} | {} |\n", q, c.evaluate(q));
    auto full = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    full.line(x, y, "prepared cubic", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(c.xs(), c.ys(),
                                                               "nodes",
                                                               {17, 24, 39}, 6).title("Complete clamped curve").x_label("query x").y_label("value");
    std::vector<double> zx, zy;
    for (int i = 0; i <= 128; ++i) {
        double q = -.2 + i * .01;
        zx.push_back(q);
        zy.push_back(c.evaluate(q));
    }
    auto zoom = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    zoom.line(zx, zy, "prepared cubic", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points({0, 1}, {0, 1},
                                                                 "nodes",
                                                                 {17, 24, 39}, 6).x_limits(-.2, 1.08).y_limits(-.5, 1.2).title("Zoom: local maximum at x=1").x_label("query x").y_label("value");
    dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(full).add(zoom).fit_panels().save_svg("build/monotone_controls.svg");
}
```
