\caption(The corrected sign-change case and finite endpoint clamps.)
\alttext(The local maximum at one is preserved; the curve is constant beyond each endpoint.)

> Contracts, conclusion and references

The prepared model owns equal-size node arrays with at least two finite entries
and strictly increasing x. It rejects invalid shape/order before interpolation,
and throws if double interval widths or secants are unrepresentable. Query
results must remain finite. Its optional input-node cap defaults to1000000; zero
disables it. This counts complete nodes, not trace bytes. Final tangents and
actual decision records are borrowed const references valid for the model's
lifetime. The one-query compatibility function uses the same model with the
optional cap disabled.

The small plateau explains shared-tangent limiting, and the original step
separates shape preservation from C2 smoothness. Reusing a prepared model costs
O(n) setup and storage, then O(log n) per query. Floating-point roundoff
remains; sampled range checks alone are not a universal proof. The method
interpolates, rather than denoises, its observations.

[Fritsch and Carlson, Monotone piecewise cubic interpolation (1980)|https://doi.org/10.1137/0717021]
gives the monotonicity framework. The arithmetic-mean initial slopes, sequential
radial limiter and endpoint policy specify this implementation.

> Verification

The ten-report batch passes95 CTest cases,31 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases,83 compiled and executed public examples,363/363 scoped documentation
definitions and ten representative hovers. Independent Python integer
arithmetic, MT19937-64/variation replay, graph sets, analytic interpolation,
circle boundary enumeration and actual-sample integration reconstruction agree
on915459 captured records. All six original RMS summaries are separately checked
using96 native MISER estimates and1600000 independently reproduced
plain-comparator points. Frozen valid-input comparisons include the original
seeded solver paths and full MOEA/D fronts. Ten checkout headers and ten
identically installed development headers compile independently, and an
installed-header native consumer links and runs. Each report has four executed
complete programs, four reviewed native figures and both HTML/Markdown exports
with computed-result and image-byte checks. This is a scoped native API audit,
not an installation claim for every language binding. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-234-243/`.
